The filings only partly answer this question. They show that Athleta weakened in fiscal 2025, but they don't explain why.

Athleta Global's comparable sales were down 9 percent in fiscal 2025, versus flat in fiscal 2024. [1] The discussion of net sales says the company's overall 2 percent increase was driven mainly by online sales, led by Old Navy Global and Gap Global, and partly offset by Athleta Global. [2] The filing also notes that less promotional activity at all brands except Athleta Global partly offset higher cost of goods sold [3], so Athleta did not cut back promotions the way the other brands did. It does not link that to Athleta's sales performance.

Athleta's store base also shrank: Athleta North America went from 260 stores to 252, a net closure of 8 in fiscal 2025. [4]

What's missing is any stated reason for the Athleta decline, such as product, demand, or competition factors specific to that brand.